rce>Realising the University in an age of supercomplexity</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Buckingham. Open University Press. UK</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramsden</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><source>Learning to teach in higher education</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>Routledge. London. UK</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B37"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hager</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonczi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Athanasou</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>The development of competency-based assessment strategies for professions National Office of Overseas Recognition research paper No8 DEET</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>Canberra: Australian Government Publishing Service</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>